  "narrative": {
    "text": "**Business & market dynamics:** GoodRx’s legacy prescription transactions business continues to face headwinds, causing overall revenue to slide year-over-year. However, the mix is rapidly improving: Pharma Direct surged on expanded manufacturer programs and GLP-1 access, while condition-specific subscriptions posted healthy growth. The business is pivoting from discount card volume toward stickier, higher-value savings models, although the transition still weighs on the top line.\n\n**Management strategy and execution:** Management raised full-year guidance, signaling confidence in the strategic shift toward Pharma Direct and subscriptions. Leadership is actively reallocating focus away from the declining core, emphasizing disciplined cost management and manufacturer partnerships. The early traction in newer streams lends some credibility, but the negative free cash flow and ongoing legacy erosion keep execution risk in focus.",
